      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence is supported: the packet states that HMA “examines how efficiently a task is accomplished, otherwise known as motion economy.”",
        "The second sentence contains substantive elements not fully supported by the packet: while the packet includes a “smoothness” feature and reports that adjusted differences between trainees and experts narrowed, it does not explicitly support the phrasing that motion economy in skill training specifically means “less excessive” movements or that it is defined as movements “closer to expert performance” in the general definitional sense used in the second sentence (it reports measured narrowing in specific probe-movement metrics over time, rather than stating this as part of the term’s definition)."
